<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African maize body calls for cheaper fertiliser.</title>
<headline>S.African maize body calls for cheaper fertiliser.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's National Maize Producers Organisation (Nampo) on Monday called for lower fertiliser prices in line with a drop in world market prices.</p>
<p>Nampo said in a statement that some farmers were still experiencing increases in fertiliser prices of 25 to 30 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;Nampo believes that fertiliser prices should now be lowered because the world market price of fertiliser dropped since the middle of last year and the (rand/dollar) exchange rate continues to strengthen,&quot; Nampo said.</p>
<p>It said cereal production in South Africa had been under increasing pressure for the past two years due to sharp increases in fertiliser prices.</p>
<p>Nampo added that fertiliser was one of the main cost factors in production.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27-11 482 1003</p>
</text>
